triage:c4_qa1_ARCH_002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "ARCH-002" ;
 triage:severity "BLOCKING" ;
 triage:reviewer "arch-qa" ;
 triage:status "author_corrected_pending_independent_review" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "53820927ccbcf174199c3042f0a07784d7fc9f0e" ;
 triage:file "template/crates/daemon/src/composition.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The selected generated root returns cron_failure before inspecting the result of run_with_cleanup. If scheduler startup succeeds, the daemon later fails to bind/serve, and consumer-provided command cleanup returns Err, the cleanup error replaces the original RuntimeError. ADR-RT-0005 decision4 requires return of the original startup/serving result after cleanup; the builder contract also explicitly permits retaining the application cleanup result separately without replacing the primary error. The SDK correctly preserves that result, but this final root discards it. This is a source ordering defect, separate from release-proof gaps; all physical joins are still awaited." ;
 triage:action "After awaited cleanup, preserve an existing daemon startup/serving error as primary. Surface cleanup failure only when the runtime result succeeded, or attach it as secondary diagnostics without losing the original error/code. Preserve the specific cron-start cause when enriching a stores failure. Verify the combined primary-error plus cleanup-error path with deterministic injection." ;
 triage:source_fix "Preserved primary SDK RuntimeError after awaited native cleanup; secondary cron failure emits safe canonical event. Four-way generated regression passes; original cleanup-first behavior causally fails." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/122#issuecomment-6677040574" .

