triage:c4_qa1_RBP_F001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "RBP-F001" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "rust-best-practices-agent" ;
 triage:status "author_corrected_pending_independent_review" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "53820927ccbcf174199c3042f0a07784d7fc9f0e" ;
 triage:file "template/crates/daemon/src/composition.rs" ;
 triage:issue "A cron cleanup failure replaces an existing primary startup/serve error at the production composition boundary. After run_with_cleanup returns, any cron_failure is returned before examining result. For example, an occupied endpoint plus a failing application command-cleanup callback reports only the cleanup error and loses the endpoint bind code, cause and recovery." ;
 triage:action "Retain the SDK startup/serve failure as primary when both it and cron shutdown fail, and report the cron cleanup failure as a secondary diagnostic after physical join. Preserve the original cron startup cause when it is the cause of the deliberately synthesized DAEMON.CRON_START stores failure. Add focused deterministic assertions for simultaneous primary/cleanup failure and cleanup-only failure." ;
 triage:source_fix "Shared production completion seam preserves primary failure, reports secondary safely and returns cleanup failure only after runtime success; focused generated regression passes." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/122#issuecomment-6677040574" .

triage:c4_qa1_RBP_F002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "RBP-F002" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "rust-best-practices-agent" ;
 triage:status "author_corrected_pending_independent_review" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "53820927ccbcf174199c3042f0a07784d7fc9f0e" ;
 triage:file "template/crates/daemon/src/composition.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The same production error formatter labels all cron failures DAEMON.CRON_OPEN and discards the native stable code and recovery. It is used for both opening failures and shutdown/custom-cleanup failures. A StoreErrorKind::Indeterminate therefore ends with generic advice to fix configuration or the database path and retry, losing the native explicit prohibition on automatic replay and separately authorized reconciliation guidance." ;
 triage:action "Format cron failures using their actual stable classification and applicable native recovery, with startup/shutdown context where helpful. Preserve the no-replay/reconciliation guidance for uncertain persistence and the lifecycle-owner guidance for shutdown failures; keep sensitive provider prose out of public diagnostics. Assert the emitted code and recovery for configuration, runtime-unavailable and indeterminate cleanup failures." ;
 triage:source_fix "Cron errors retain native code and static recovery with value-free causes and typed transaction facts. Indeterminate keeps separately authorized reconciliation/no automatic replay; provider source/context redacted." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/122#issuecomment-6677040574" .

triage:c4_qa1_FTQ_001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-001" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "author_corrected_pending_independent_review" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "53820927ccbcf174199c3042f0a07784d7fc9f0e" ;
 triage:file "tests/integration/generation/owned_process.py" ;
 triage:issue "Carry-forward correlation REQ-C5-008, not a new tracker request: after actual command launch, ps inspection failure in _session_listing raises before enumerating descendants. finally kills only the launcher process group. A ready descendant in another process group of the same session survives; child.wait confirms only the launcher, and TemporaryDirectory exits without physical descendant completion. Preflight inspection does not prevent later inspection failures." ;
 triage:action "Consume the C5 owner repair with a causal postlaunch inspection-failure witness retaining descendant identity and ownership through physical exit; fail accurately without assuming leader/group termination proves session completion." ;
 triage:source_fix "Canonical shared owner source consumed; composed Python owner tests include physically cleaned postlaunch inspection and distinct-group descendants." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/122#issuecomment-6677040574" .

triage:c4_qa1_FTQ_002 a triage:Finding ;
